  "scope": "A formation is classified by its relation to the conditions of the relations it participates in (dependence or drawing): renewing when each such condition keeps supporting every formation depending on it, consuming when it draws on a condition some dependent formation permanently loses. Exclusive, not exhaustive. Unrenewed drawdown admits finitely many active steps. In a law where the renewing formation depends on the condition it renews: within renewal, continuation and unbounded formation; beyond renewal, permanent loss of the renewer's support, self-ending with bounded formation for a dependent focal formation, and unbounded persistence for an independent one. Neither formation at each active step nor the focal formation's own trajectory decides the class; joint drawing can consume when each alone is within renewal; escalation beginning within renewal consumes. No ethical predicate; every declaration is required to have an empty axiom set. Levels, needs and rates are local representations whose real correspondence is not established.",
